# 🐳 Step 3 – Verify Docker Installation

Check Docker.

```bash
docker --version
```

Example

```text
Docker version 28.x
```

Check Docker Compose.

```bash
docker compose version
```

If you receive

```text
docker: 'compose' is not a docker command
```

> [!WARNING]
> Docker Compose plugin is missing. Install or update Docker Desktop.

---

# ⚙️ Step 4 – Review Docker Compose

Open the compose file.

```bash
cat docker-compose.yml
```

Example

```yaml
services:

  mysql:
    image: mysql:8.0

  backend:
    build: ./backend

  frontend:
    build: ./frontend
```

This creates three services.

| Service     | Purpose       |
| ----------- | ------------- |
| 🗄️ MySQL   | Database      |
| 🟢 Backend  | Node.js API   |
| ⚛️ Frontend | React + Nginx |

---

# 🔐 Step 5 – Configure Environment Variables

Verify the environment file.

```bash
ls -la
```

If missing,

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Edit

```bash
nano .env
```

Example

```env
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=root123
DB_NAME=devops_exam_db
DB_USER=exam_user
DB_PASSWORD=password
PORT=5001
```

> [!TIP]
> Docker Compose automatically loads values from the `.env` file.

