# 🔍 Step 12 – Debug Login Failure

Follow the request path.

```mermaid
flowchart LR

Browser --> Frontend
Frontend --> Backend
Backend --> Database
```

Check backend logs.

```bash
docker compose logs -f backend
```

If no login request appears,

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The request never reached the backend.

The issue exists before the backend.

---

# 🔧 Step 13 – Verify Nginx Configuration

Search for API configuration.

```bash
grep -R "api\|5001\|localhost" frontend/
```

Found

```nginx
proxy_pass http://backend:5000/api/;
```

Problem

Backend runs on

```text
5001
```

but Nginx points to

```text
5000
```

---

# ✅ Step 14 – Confirm Using Logs

```bash
docker compose logs frontend
```

Example

```text
POST /api/auth/login

upstream:
backend:5000

connection refused
```

Root cause identified.

❌ Wrong backend port.

---

# 🔄 Step 15 – Fix the Configuration

Replace

```nginx
proxy_pass http://backend:5000/api/;
```

with

```nginx
proxy_pass http://backend:5001/api/;
```

Rebuild

```bash
docker compose up -d --build frontend
```

---

# 🗄️ Step 16 – Verify Database

Connect to MySQL

```bash
docker compose exec mysql mysql -u root -p
```

Useful commands

```sql
SHOW DATABASES;

USE devops_exam_db;

SHOW TABLES;

SELECT * FROM results;
```

